         <notesStmt>
            <note type="project" target="#dat1">Of two very similar corrected proofs (see yal.00034), this was probably created later, as it contains a slightly more comlplete set of corrections. It probably dates to early <date when="1884">1884</date>, shortly before the poem was published in <hi rend="italic">Harper's Monthly</hi>.</note>
            <note type="work_relations" target="xxx.00340" cert="high">"With Husky-Haughty Lips, O Sea!" was published first in the March 1884 issue of <hi rend="italic">Harper's Monthly Magazine</hi>. It was reprinted, with the addition of one line, in <hi rend="italic">November Boughs</hi> (1888) and in the "Sands at Seventy" annex to <hi rend="italic">Leaves of Grass</hi> in 1888 and after.</note>
         </notesStmt>
